# llama.cpp — environment
# Copy to `.env` and adjust:  cp .env.example .env
#
# NOTE: COMPOSE_PROFILES does NOT belong here — it selects which of the two
# services (llama-cuda / llama-vulkan) exists, and Compose only reads it from the
# project root .env or the shell. Setting it in this file does nothing at all.
# Run ./detect-gpu.sh, which writes it to ../.env.
#
# ---- Required ----
# Host directory holding your GGUF weights. Mounted read-only at /models.
LLAMA_MODELS_DIR=/home/ahill/.lmstudio/models/lmstudio-community
#
# Model file to load, as a path *relative to* LLAMA_MODELS_DIR above.
LLAMA_MODEL=gemma-4-E4B-it-GGUF/gemma-4-E4B-it-Q4_K_M.gguf
#
# ---- Image pin ----
# Rolling tags by default (see compose.yml). Pin to a build tag once the box is
# in service. The two backends are separate images from the same commit, so both
# carry the same build number; only the profile Compose selects is ever pulled.
#
# b10752 is the newest build ghcr publishes an image for. Images exist for only a
# subset of build tags — b10753 through b10760 are git tags with no image — so
# verify before bumping:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp:server-vulkan-bNNNNN
LLAMA_CUDA_IMAGE_TAG=server-cuda-b10752
LLAMA_VULKAN_IMAGE_TAG=server-vulkan-b10752
#
# ---- Optional ----
# Layers offloaded to the GPU. 999 means all of them. Lower it if the model does
# not fit in VRAM — on an integrated GPU that shares system memory, all-in usually
# works, on a small discrete card it may not.
# LLAMA_NGL=999
#
# Context window in tokens. Costs memory; drop it if the server fails to allocate.
# LLAMA_CTX=16384
